<body><main style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding:40px 20px"><h1>faq</h1>
<h2>Do I need a Google Cloud project? No.</h2>
<p>Download Sift, create an app password on your Google account, paste it in. No consoles, no client IDs, no verification screens.</p>
<h2>Is an app password safe?</h2>
<p>Google lets you give one app its own password instead of your real one. It only works for Sift, you can revoke it any time on the same page, and Sift keeps it in your Mac's Keychain. Nothing is sent anywhere except Google.</p>
<p>Run it yourself: <code>brew install ownpath/tap/sift-bench</code> then <code>sift-bench quick</code>.</p>
